course: dictionary
lesson: 5873
title: Meaning in context: mane
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mane is a noun, so it names a thing. You may meet it in a story about a lion or a horse. Look at the clues around it: «Przewalski's horses are short and stocky, sandy brown, with a stiff mane that stands up like a brush.» A stiff thing that stands up like a brush is hair, so a mane must be hair growing somewhere on the animal.
explain: Now find where the mane is. «A mane makes a lion look bigger and protects his neck in fights.» The clue is in the neck. A mane is the long, thick hair on the neck of some animals. Try your meaning in the sentence: «A long, thick hair on the neck makes a lion look bigger.» It still makes sense, so you have it.
explain: The plural is manes. Watch out for «the lion's mane jellyfish». Here mane is part of a name. The jellyfish is not a lion and does not have a mane. The name only borrows the word.
fact: A mane is the long, thick hair growing on the neck of some animals, especially horses and male lions.
fact: Informally, a person's long, thick hair can be called a mane, as in «a mane of red hair».
fact: Only male lions grow manes, and a dark, full mane shows a lion is healthy.
fact: A mane makes a lion look bigger and protects his neck in fights.
fact: Useful phrases: a lion's mane, a horse's mane, a mane of hair.
exercise: «Only male lions grow manes.» What is a mane? | *The long, thick hair growing on the neck of some animals | A tail that swishes at flies | A kind of rock | A small wild cat
exercise: «Przewalski's horses have a stiff mane that stands up like a brush.» Find and copy the word for the hair on the horse's neck. | *mane | stands | brush | stiff
exercise: The sentence «a mane of red hair» is informal. What does mane mean when it describes a person? | A cap worn in the cold | *Long, thick hair | A red paint | A cold wind
test: «A mane makes a lion look bigger and protects his neck in fights.» What does the mane do for a lion? | Makes it swim faster | Helps it climb trees | Makes it lay eggs | *Makes it look bigger and protects its neck
test: «A dark full mane shows he is healthy.» Which lion may be healthy? | A lion with a thin mane | *A lion with a dark, full mane | A lion with no mane | A lion with a short tail
exam: «The big golden male with his mane roars across the plain.» In this sentence, what is a mane? | A roar at dawn | A cave on the plain | A kind of grass | *The long, thick hair on the neck of the male lion
